#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078179 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078421 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "839431c8-b292-5ed9-b549-2d81b12df45b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Arithmetic Sequence"}] :question/id #uuid "eba75ca0-7f78-531f-96c4-b772b5785828" :question/math-academy-id "e-14375" :question/problem "Which of the three sequences below are arithmetic sequences?\n\nI. $2, \\: 4, \\: 6, \\: 8, \\: \\ldots$\n\nII. $5, \\: 2, \\: -1, \\: -4, \\: \\ldots$\n\nIII. $2, \\: 5, \\: 8, \\: 12, \\: \\ldots$" :question/worked-solution "To determine whether each sequence is an arithmetic sequence, we need to look at the jumps between terms in the sequence. If the jumps are the same, then they indeed represent a common difference of an arithmetic sequence.\n\n- In sequence I, the jumps are all the same. Therefore, sequence I is an arithmetic sequence with common difference $d=2.$\n\n![](images/17/17933a1cabd8d487dd1607f7ae7064d6e186e3454a52497977f866150c491f25.png)\n\n- In sequence II, the jumps are all the same. Therefore, sequence II is an arithmetic sequence with common difference $d=-3.$\n\n![](images/9d/9d9a41035215deb27d0578123a859d9b492b505d79b0a0a71f62c822942298ca.png)\n\n- In sequence III, the jumps are not all the same. Therefore, sequence III is not an arithmetic sequence.\n\n![](images/2b/2b860338be6ff8876c1368ed5f08162096873fa9992a9e88d7ff545752a5bd36.png)\n\nIn conclusion, only sequences I and II are arithmetic sequences."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078180 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078422 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "73efb24d-e21f-5999-b545-2e3539440735" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Terms of an Arithmetic Sequence"}] :question/id #uuid "510e7581-c8f5-51b0-931b-02f6e926e5f2" :question/math-academy-id "e-14381" :question/problem "What is the $8$th term of the following arithmetic sequence?\n\n$$\n4, \\: 7, \\: 10, \\: 13, \\: 16, \\: \\ldots\n$$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/ac/ac878a3d258fa19641d983863580af953bbea593b49bffff16f2f09eb7b6ab2d.png)\n\nWe notice that the sequence is an arithmetic sequence with a common difference of \n\n$$\nd=7-4=3.\n$$\n\nSo, we can calculate each term in the sequence by adding $3$ to the previous term. \n\nWe will continue listing terms of the sequence until we get to the $8$th term. Listing the terms up to the $8$th term, we have:\n\n![](images/e5/e536739b28db7d0f221967ce8729eee502a29f80caec8e1c39f61a9cfe4a6459.png)\n\nTherefore, the $8$th term is $25.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078194 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078420 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ac161f82-668f-5e67-b8d8-c2f6a438c7a8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Common Difference"}] :question/id #uuid "ae7753b6-b58d-57c5-849e-c887e7d1601e" :question/math-academy-id "e-14731" :question/problem "What is the common difference of the following arithmetic sequence?\n\n$$\n7,\\: 2,\\: -3,\\: -8,\\: \\ldots\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The common difference $d$ of an arithmetic sequence is the difference between any two consecutive terms.\n\nTherefore, the common difference for our sequence is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={a}_{2}-{a}_{1} \\\\  & =2-7 \\\\  & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519560 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078421 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "839431c8-b292-5ed9-b549-2d81b12df45b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Arithmetic Sequence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9ae2ab66-e8cf-5ba6-85d1-13ea1914a405" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519249} {:answer/id #uuid "9e210bae-211c-59b1-92d0-fc04eb55e1e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519251} {:answer/id #uuid "a28412fa-c9d8-5d99-a377-d20b7d99d741" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519260} {:answer/id #uuid "cc568d89-df8b-57de-99ef-c6cc9273d3ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519325} {:answer/id #uuid "de35765a-9e00-5086-b227-e972d3a9760d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519357}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "de35765a-9e00-5086-b227-e972d3a9760d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519357} :answer-field/id #uuid "002ab7e3-3e7c-58af-a8be-ddecace186b6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519414}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8dd21bc7-cc1c-556a-83c5-25089927d9b3" :question/math-academy-id "q-100790" :question/problem "Which of the three sequences below are arithmetic sequences?\n\nI. $-2,\\,-4,\\,-6,\\,-8,...$\n\nII. $-2,\\,-9,\\,-16,\\,-23,...$\n\nIII. $-2,\\,4,\\,10,\\,16,...$" :question/worked-solution "To determine whether each sequence is an arithmetic sequence, we need to look at the jumps between terms in the sequence. If the jumps are the same, then they indeed represent a common difference of an arithmetic sequence. \n\n- In sequence I, the jumps are all the same. Therefore, sequence I is an arithmetic sequence with common difference $d=-2.$\n\n![](images/c5/c599604e6630b0dbf74d646f93b6330b5d310f35bfbce7b008f16d1686534c77.png)\n\n- In sequence II, the jumps are all the same. Therefore, sequence II is an arithmetic sequence with common difference $d=-7.$\n\n![](images/b3/b35cc27bfa6f7fe2171529a0c84e9ab8d33c122e932512fae1b06fe21cc9bc94.png)\n\n- In sequence III, the jumps are all the same. Therefore, sequence III is an arithmetic sequence with common difference $d=6.$\n\n![](images/9a/9aa43107c2b5c975450590f4bc126273b45ddc72f1acfd3d35eadff0313ded1b.png)\n\nIn conclusion, sequences I, II, and III are arithmetic sequences."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519579 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078422 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "73efb24d-e21f-5999-b545-2e3539440735" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Terms of an Arithmetic Sequence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e16fd4a-6245-515d-bca9-21c581bb11c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519039} {:answer/id #uuid "37e257f1-1b06-5206-b1e4-0f6fd61394c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519077} {:answer/id #uuid "839bdee5-429a-5249-b53f-0d20a4a67a86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519197} {:answer/id #uuid "8dc1a3d5-cb5c-5204-a75d-1ad43a7bc92b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519224} {:answer/id #uuid "ec9bbfcd-9965-5de5-905a-9f1ee62878ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519380}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "839bdee5-429a-5249-b53f-0d20a4a67a86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519197} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab00a963-1cd0-5605-a266-0b494ab59620" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519476}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b7af1a90-ae65-5ea4-82bf-4487562443e4" :question/math-academy-id "q-19977" :question/problem "Find the third term of an arithmetic sequence if the first term is $23$ and the common difference is $-7.$" :question/worked-solution "We will list terms of the sequence until we get to the third term. \n\nWe start with the first term $23,$ and then we calculate each subsequent term by subtracting $7$ from the previous term:\n\n![](images/86/86fe86315966ba57e674e652510c2814ab94f0cf8869656c9fa3b7c934801b9f.png)\n\nTherefore, the third term is $9.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519527 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078420 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ac161f82-668f-5e67-b8d8-c2f6a438c7a8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Common Difference"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e72b408f-9678-5df5-8e3c-c25bf6966626" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519372}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e72b408f-9678-5df5-8e3c-c25bf6966626" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519372} :answer-field/id #uuid "d52aac11-c9ed-51ba-b011-6d52463e90a6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519497}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "201f78ad-e932-54f4-94ee-8dd6f6a1154d" :question/math-academy-id "q-215844" :question/problem "Consider the following arithmetic sequence.\n\n$$\n-22,\\,-31,\\,-40,\\,-49,\\,…\n$$\n\nThe common difference of this arithmetic sequence is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The common difference $d$ of an arithmetic sequence is the difference between any two consecutive terms.\n\nTherefore, the common difference for our sequence is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={a}_{2}-{a}_{1} \\\\  & =-31-(-22) \\\\  & =-31+22 \\\\  & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078883 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078421 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "839431c8-b292-5ed9-b549-2d81b12df45b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Arithmetic Sequence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae56415c-614e-5010-84b2-152c6dbf8e7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186076077} {:answer/id #uuid "0007cb31-26a9-5baa-bb56-3315e50f92d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186076078} {:answer/id #uuid "5423d064-430d-5df3-844e-c5b95a86e210" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186076079} {:answer/id #uuid "573eb60d-c9a8-5e53-86cf-c5b203b832ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186076080} {:answer/id #uuid "57aa2166-1627-5c3f-b2d3-eb4cdfbc2479" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186076081}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5423d064-430d-5df3-844e-c5b95a86e210" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186076079} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ddb97aa-753c-55ab-a316-b6f60bf556c5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186076076}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d14404fc-deb2-5ffc-b0b6-821e376bc0d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-39107" :question/problem "Which of the three sequences below are arithmetic sequences?\n\nI. $6,10,14,18,...$\n\nII. $4,8,16,32,...$\n\nIII. $87,74,61,46,...$" :question/worked-solution "To determine whether each sequence is an arithmetic sequence, we need to look at the jumps between terms in the sequence. If the jumps are the same, then they indeed represent a common difference of an arithmetic sequence.\n\n- In sequence I, the jumps are all the same. Therefore, sequence I is an arithmetic sequence with common difference $d=4.$\n\n![](images/bb/bbb6555443ed4fdf7f29da4571d421b833fb21e2556a440d821bbd4e4b986923.png)\n\n- In sequence II, the jumps are not all the same. Therefore, sequence II is not an arithmetic sequence.\n\n![](images/64/6408dd510dd59615c69c063897a6ff483c20bc485d73164e74c2f57dacc4dce8.png)\n\n- In sequence III, the jumps are not all the same. Therefore, sequence III is not an arithmetic sequence.\n\n![](images/24/246210488611eed52df8d3e777e296bff30889c7dd8122d082c5d4a6bb6d7ad6.png)\n\nIn conclusion, only sequence I is an arithmetic sequence."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519586 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078422 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "73efb24d-e21f-5999-b545-2e3539440735" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Terms of an Arithmetic Sequence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48471eaf-485b-57e4-b57e-a735e38e449c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519106} {:answer/id #uuid "afe020d8-2c1b-5283-b62d-5b9d95e3a369" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519278} {:answer/id #uuid "cde37cbf-59b7-560e-bdf2-a97cdc9cc8af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519327} {:answer/id #uuid "e026946b-e444-5c11-ad1d-2bed1dc460f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519362} {:answer/id #uuid "f213e393-5ca9-51a1-86ce-6d826b129fa7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519392}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "48471eaf-485b-57e4-b57e-a735e38e449c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519106} :answer-field/id #uuid "81579da1-4713-52e7-82a4-48a156d67a53" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519458}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d4919d08-0fd6-56c9-962f-b38905295542" :question/math-academy-id "q-5260" :question/problem "Find the fourth term of an arithmetic sequence if the first term is $1$ and the common difference is $-2.$" :question/worked-solution "We will list terms of the sequence until we get to the fourth term. \n\nWe start with the first term $1,$ and then we calculate each subsequent term by subtracting $2$ from the previous term:\n\n![](images/2f/2f8e4976e5ea05c0d238959425d4d2d5ece23d4bfae844e533e9eb484f9de18a.png)\n\nTherefore, the fourth term is $-5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519574 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078420 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ac161f82-668f-5e67-b8d8-c2f6a438c7a8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Common Difference"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "92bf199e-afa9-59a0-99c5-39dc96c0e3eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519233} {:answer/id #uuid "98ceb62e-64c1-53d3-898f-8c9877f2dbac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519243} {:answer/id #uuid "b6c3c789-1301-5acb-8ade-6ed3fe3ea32e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519292} {:answer/id #uuid "bf290a1a-2ea6-5f25-a62a-e7695091261d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519306} {:answer/id #uuid "f8f2817a-212b-5b87-9b74-644f72a88914" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519404}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "92bf199e-afa9-59a0-99c5-39dc96c0e3eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519233} :answer-field/id #uuid "68361dd6-1e8b-506a-8578-5b4e969159f0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519449}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a8cf8516-d7bc-5fa0-86d7-e74e836777c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-67189" :question/problem "What is the common difference for the following arithmetic sequence?\n\n$$\n-5,\\,-12,\\,-19,\\,-26,\\,…\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The common difference $d$ of an arithmetic sequence is the difference between any two consecutive terms.\n\nTherefore, the common difference for our sequence is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={a}_{2}-{a}_{1} \\\\  & =-12-(-5) \\\\  & =-7\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
